# Pre-Flight line-ending rules.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which silently converts
#   LF -> CRLF on checkout and CRLF -> LF on commit, and prints a warning
#   every time it touches a file ("LF will be replaced by CRLF..."). The
#   warnings are noisy and the silent conversion can confuse tools that
#   expect deterministic byte content (Prettier, ESLint, hashes in tests).
#
# What this file does:
#   1. Pins every text file to LF endings in the repository AND in the
#      working copy. No conversion happens on checkout or commit.
#   2. Prevents Git from misclassifying binary assets (SVGs treated as
#      text but PNG / WOFF / TTF treated as binary).
#   3. Applies for every contributor regardless of their local
#      core.autocrlf setting — .gitattributes always wins.
#
# After this file lands, run `git add --renormalize .` once to re-stage
# every tracked file with the new rules. Future commits stay clean.

# --- Default: treat as text, normalize to LF on commit AND checkout ---
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Source files: explicit LF ---
*.js          text eol=lf
*.jsx         text eol=lf
*.mjs         text eol=lf
*.cjs         text eol=lf
*.ts          text eol=lf
*.tsx         text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.html        text eol=lf
*.css         text eol=lf
*.scss        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.toml        text eol=lf
*.svg         text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf

# --- Config files (root-level, no extension) ---
.gitignore    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.eslintrc*    text eol=lf
.prettierrc*  text eol=lf
.editorconfig text eol=lf
.npmrc        text eol=lf
.env*         text eol=lf
LICENSE       text eol=lf
LICENSE-DATA  text eol=lf
README        text eol=lf
CLAUDE        text eol=lf

# --- Cloudflare Pages routing files ---
_redirects    text eol=lf
_headers      text eol=lf

# --- Binaries: never normalize ---
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.gif         binary
*.ico         binary
*.webp        binary
*.avif        binary
*.woff        binary
*.woff2       binary
*.ttf         binary
*.otf         binary
*.eot         binary
*.mp3         binary
*.mp4         binary
*.webm        binary
*.pdf         binary
*.zip         binary
*.tar.gz      binary
*.tgz         binary

# --- Linguist hints (GitHub's language-detection on the repo page) ---
# Mark the Learn corpus as documentation so it doesn't dominate the
# "this repo is mostly Markdown" language stat. The repo is a JS app
# that happens to ship documentation; the stat should reflect that.
src/learn/**/*.md linguist-documentation
docs/**/*.md      linguist-documentation
*.md              linguist-documentation
